{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "generation_contexts": [{"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03QW:paragraph/0006", "hash": "sha256:2c94c09b5ecd0f37ebb49a8a5b86fd48eb25f2410c9b37a533115d3c3ee0463e", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 316149, "byte_start": 315724, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:7204410a3fee9a1e78998ec5ed4cd89dac4be7eee4efe0dcc01796af244823b5", "line_end": 8623, "line_start": 8613}, "owner_tag": "03QW", "parent_tag": "03QW", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "03QW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\text{Gal}_{\\kappa(s)}$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\Sh(S_\\etale) \\longrightarrow\n\\text{Gal}_{\\kappa(s)}\\textit{-Sets},\n\\quad\n\\mathcal{F} \\longmapsto \\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}}\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{pione-definition-G-set-continuous}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:240bb3245b759a2e9f6553dc7e3fd1d7c743364585a3dd64d91cb8d97ecec144", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:71e13f7f8663af8f59d403ca15974c8f96916918b6b78456604ae892c742231d", "source_text": "Altogether we see that <MATH_0001> becomes a\n<MATH_0002>-set (see\nFundamental Groups, Definition <REF_0001>).\nHence we may think of the stalk functor as a functor\n<MATH_0003>\nand from now on we usually do think about the stalk functor in this way.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:516eb109a7f865ff958994074e10b201ce1c86dc05523085ba0f6e6fc61a2c56", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03QW:paragraph/0006"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03QT:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:69992216ac3a4dcbf6bc76b2044e60283febda0941826c3c22ad7efda97a648d", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 317147, "byte_start": 316538, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:508c1184ed891db90b6b82e0b1e0d6404aaeba04ac2be9ecd55cfcb5aabd0760", "line_end": 8651, "line_start": 8638}, "owner_tag": "03QT", "parent_tag": "03QW", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03QW", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "MATH_0001": "$G$", "MATH_0002": "$M$", "MATH_0003": "$X \\to \\Spec(K)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Mor_K(\\Spec(K^{sep}), X)$", "MATH_0005": "$M$", "MATH_0006": "$G$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Spec(K)_\\etale$", "MATH_0009": "$U \\mapsto \\Mor_K(U, X)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}} = \\Mor_K(\\Spec(K^{sep}), X) = M$", "MATH_0011": "$G$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{pione-lemma-sheaves-point}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:edbf1f580c8410b133e59b5abbac7250bb6305d1d2411f235b75f0c2e9323200", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:883ae901744aaa8afdf5a4f996ab97e4c78c6d08a7c5b08a6a8cfd40a1c7f8d3", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nLet us construct the inverse to this functor. In\nFundamental Groups, Lemma <REF_0001>\nwe have seen that given a <MATH_0001>-set <MATH_0002> there exists an <ACCENT_0001>tale morphism\n<MATH_0003>\nsuch that <MATH_0004> is\nisomorphic to <MATH_0005> as a <MATH_0006>-set. Consider the sheaf\n<MATH_0007> on <MATH_0008> defined by\nthe rule <MATH_0009>. This is a sheaf as the <ACCENT_0002>tale\ntopology is subcanonical. Then we see that\n<MATH_0010>\nas <MATH_0011>-sets (details omitted). This gives the inverse of the functor and\nwe win.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:590abfe1209c90ec2f08f0aaf2cfbcf283d73222ca24444b304a589fcd28b108", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03QT:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:03QT:theorem/0001", "hash": "sha256:2ac4c603cb1de33f6228ea1c1efc3e8a29acf5e0cc6e34be151fa33f73d3127a", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 316536, "byte_start": 316151, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:e88f70cc33688318d10b0b2e667c890ef5283297b44c538ef7015c68d8515df2", "line_end": 8636, "line_start": 8625}, "owner_tag": "03QT", "parent_tag": "03QW", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "theorem", "parent_tag": "03QW", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}", "MATH_0001": "$S = \\Spec(K)$", "MATH_0002": "$K$", "MATH_0003": "$\\overline{s}$", "MATH_0004": "$S$", "MATH_0005": "$G = \\text{Gal}_{\\kappa(s)}$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\Sh(S_\\etale) \\longrightarrow G\\textit{-Sets},\n\\quad\n\\mathcal{F} \\longmapsto \\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}}.\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{theorem}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{theorem}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:826cf88935baac33e510fd0c760b3b78a49270724891ba9f6645509a2b654db2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c12aa9a839ac62fb06daec35abea0cb1018066445df10ff4461dc87cc26eb350", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> with <MATH_0002> a field.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a geometric point of <MATH_0004>.\nLet <MATH_0005> denote the absolute Galois group.\nTaking stalks induces an equivalence of categories\n<MATH_0006>\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3a18742e85a86b8762a15d7dc9422fd31a6a0d1a5beec7900968cf52d83ae5c2", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:03QT:theorem/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:04JL:remark/0001", "hash": "sha256:86a66ccd98b3d2c92ab2d3a6a438d327093682ef6eb0460dbd56be07ab02932f", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 317791, "byte_start": 317149, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:bf09e241cb19a151a6d336b7258150f56b90fa94fdb3a752e39ae649228f914b", "line_end": 8665, "line_start": 8653}, "owner_tag": "04JL", "parent_tag": "03QW", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "03QW", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "LOCKED_0001": "\\label{remark-every-sheaf-representable}", "MATH_0001": "$\\Spec(K)_\\etale$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Spec(K)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\Spec(K)_\\etale$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Spec(K)$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(K)_\\etale$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{pione-lemma-sheaves-point}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-definition-representable-sheaf}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{remark}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{remark}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ff4484f9db6a69d8020f1ab62d01c8633ed85ff42f05e2be7a80da82864c7e1f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:da323a9ed2a75aec7fd9bcdf8c91add29ec2286f7c698b9c6e12e330e7d3b3bd", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nAnother way to state the conclusion of\nTheorem <REF_0001> and\nFundamental Groups, Lemma <REF_0002>\nis to say that every sheaf on <MATH_0001> is representable\nby a scheme <MATH_0002> <ACCENT_0001>tale over <MATH_0003>.\nThis does not mean that every sheaf is representable in the sense of\nSites, Definition <REF_0003>.\nThe reason is that in our construction of <MATH_0004>\nwe chose a sufficiently large set of schemes <ACCENT_0002>tale over <MATH_0005>,\nwhereas sheaves on <MATH_0006> form a proper class.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1125463bccb4a84947920d482fbc049a20b4407bf3053cf36e3fbbbeedd4ae60", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:04JL:remark/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:04JM:lemma/0001", "hash": "sha256:da899233b0e31f5079459888371f811af2d1fa65176c40b0e627266bcdd60758", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 318029, "byte_start": 317793, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:cc815de35168f6b89f26c20de466bc262acbbb4d32bd73c641cfa9220ff12f41", "line_end": 8675, "line_start": 8667}, "owner_tag": "04JM", "parent_tag": "03QW", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "03QW", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-global-sections-point}", "MATH_0001": "$$\n\\Gamma(S, \\mathcal{F}) = (\\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}})^G\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{lemma}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{lemma}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:d550ecfe3e9af773a459da9dde465f13bdf20f6881a8563f7a2219b684d16e17", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:9c3be3ef42d49bb9094f1ad370a550afda84ea915ff8308d0c3d524a5cd2a505", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nAssumptions and notations as in\nTheorem <REF_0001>.\nThere is a functorial bijection\n<MATH_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4fddffb253b06d4c1c0f5be6523bfb6f11c428e0a7b410c073ff4fab2c084932", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:04JM:lemma/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-neighbor:etale-cohomology:inventory:etale-cohomology:04JM:proof/0001", "hash": "sha256:483114496560c38443ce5a5d48516326e1264f9ed9e2a7df1475aed92965e127", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 320367, "byte_start": 318031, "file": "etale-cohomology.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:165411d23bd61c894e6da5a942dfbdaae0b1838e30b7bb0b89e26828ed2a1c29", "line_end": 8729, "line_start": 8677}, "owner_tag": "04JM", "parent_tag": "03QW", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "etale-cohomology", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "03QW", "placeholders": {"ACCENT_0001": "\\'e", "ACCENT_0002": "\\'e", "FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$G$", "MATH_0003": "$M = \\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}}$", "MATH_0004": "\\begin{eqnarray*}\n\\Gamma(S, \\mathcal{F}) & = &\n\\Mor_{\\Sh(S_\\etale)}(h_{\\Spec(K)},  \\mathcal{F})\n\\\\\n& = & \\Mor_{G\\textit{-Sets}}(\\{*\\}, M) \\\\\n& = & M^G\n\\end{eqnarray*}", "MATH_0005": "$t \\in \\Gamma(S, \\mathcal{F})$", "MATH_0006": "$(S, \\overline{s}, t)$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}}$", "MATH_0008": "$G$", "MATH_0009": "$(U, \\overline{u}, t)$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}}$", "MATH_0011": "$U$", "MATH_0012": "$U = \\Spec(L)$", "MATH_0013": "$K$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}_{\\overline{s}}$", "MATH_0015": "$(U', \\overline{u}') \\to (U, \\overline{u})$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{F}(U) \\to \\mathcal{F}(U')$", "MATH_0017": "$U' \\to U$", "MATH_0018": "$S_\\etale$", "MATH_0019": "$L$", "MATH_0020": "$K \\subset L$", "MATH_0021": "$$\n\\Spec(L) \\times_{\\Spec(K)} \\Spec(L)\n=\n\\coprod\\nolimits_{\\sigma \\in \\text{Gal}(L/K)} \\Spec(L)\n$$", "MATH_0022": "$\\Spec(L) \\to \\Spec(L \\otimes_K L)$", "MATH_0023": "$a \\otimes b \\mapsto a\\sigma(b)$", "MATH_0024": "$(U, \\overline{u}, t)$", "MATH_0025": "$G$", "MATH_0026": "$t \\in \\mathcal{F}(\\Spec(L))$", "MATH_0027": "$\\mathcal{F}(\\Spec(L) \\times_{\\Spec(K)} \\Spec(L))$", "MATH_0028": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0029": "$\\{\\Spec(L) \\to \\Spec(K)\\}$", "MATH_0030": "$t$", "MATH_0031": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0032": "$\\Spec(K)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{sites-section-presheaves}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{sites-section-representable-sheaves}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{theorem-equivalence-sheaves-point}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{proposition-etale-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e5023cb8b1b88a7e9b951408637ca81e82d1393a606eda241811910ba439fc85", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4b78f1d7a02a30d271d67c4aa0b64d501df360fd62d1f1e2362c18efb4f40268", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nWe can prove this using formal arguments and the result of\nTheorem <REF_0001>\nas follows. Given a sheaf <MATH_0001> corresponding to\nthe <MATH_0002>-set <MATH_0003> we have\n<MATH_0004>\nHere the first identification is explained in\nSites, Sections <REF_0002> and\n<REF_0003>,\nthe second results from\nTheorem <REF_0004>\nand the third is clear. We will also give a direct proof<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>For\nthe doubting Thomases out there.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nSuppose that <MATH_0005> is a global section.\nThen the triple <MATH_0006> defines an element of\n<MATH_0007> which is clearly invariant under the\naction of <MATH_0008>. Conversely, suppose that <MATH_0009>\ndefines an element of <MATH_0010> which is invariant.\nThen we may shrink <MATH_0011> and assume <MATH_0012> for some\nfinite separable field extension of <MATH_0013>, see\nProposition <REF_0005>.\nIn this case the map <MATH_0014>\nis injective, because for any morphism of <ACCENT_0001>tale neighbourhoods\n<MATH_0015> the restriction map\n<MATH_0016> is injective since <MATH_0017>\nis a covering of <MATH_0018>.\nAfter enlarging <MATH_0019> a bit we may assume <MATH_0020> is a finite\nGalois extension. At this point we use that\n<MATH_0021>\nwhere the maps <MATH_0022>\ncome from the ring maps <MATH_0023>. Hence we\nsee that the condition that <MATH_0024> is invariant\nunder all of <MATH_0025> implies that <MATH_0026>\nmaps to the same element of\n<MATH_0027>\nvia restriction by either projection (this uses the injectivity mentioned\nabove; details omitted). Hence the sheaf condition of <MATH_0028>\nfor the <ACCENT_0002>tale covering <MATH_0029> kicks\nin and we conclude that <MATH_0030> comes from a unique section of <MATH_0031>\nover <MATH_0032>.\n<STRUCT_0004>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:719c9fad1a5eb2d4a78aa68cb9245415ee5ddf7eca75f6d0d46a73e00a0e17ce", "unit_id": "inventory:etale-cohomology:04JM:proof/0001"}}}, {"context_id": "locked-English-reference:pione:inventory:pione:03QR:lemma/0001:pione-lemma-sheaves-point", "hash": "sha256:efcd4e5b61769c330a3c7e62f18fb8d28a90d80c05133f8a370998a9ab4be520", "value": {"kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 2197, "byte_start": 1818, "file": "pione.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:9f72b6d35637003d476af61b4a96b85d67e49bda76c465c2ff3f5d0486b0b466", "line_end": 83, "line_start": 68}, "owner_tag": "03QR", "parent_tag": "04JI", "requested_label": "pione-lemma-sheaves-point", "requested_tag": "03QR", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "pione", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "04JI", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{lemma-sheaves-point}", "MATH_0001": "$K$", "MATH_0002": "$K^{sep}$", "MATH_0003": "$K$", "MATH_0004": "$G = \\text{Gal}(K^{sep}/K)$", "MATH_0005": "$$\n\\begin{matrix}\n\\text{schemes \\'etale over }K &\n\\longrightarrow &\nG\\textit{-Sets} \\\\\nX/K & \\longmapsto &\n\\Mor_{\\Spec(K)}(\\Spec(K^{sep}), X)\n\\end{matrix}\n$$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin